#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:19
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Much like physical media, there are many ways to mix colors together in "
"Krita. Traditional painters and illustrators often use techniques like "
"**glazing**, **scumbling**, and **hatching** to mix colors directly on their "
"canvas, on top of mixing colors together on a **palette** or even within the "
"hairs of their **brush**. With a little bit of practice and know-how, and "
"thanks to the variety of powerful tools in Krita, we can mimic all of these "
"mixing techniques in digital painting."
msgstr ""
"Podobno kot fizični mediji, obstaja veliko načinov za mešanje barv skupaj v "
"Krita. Tradicionalni slikarji in ilustratorji pogosto uporabljajo tehnike, "
"kot so **zasteklitev**, **scumbling**, in **vali** za mešanje barv "
"neposredno na svojem platnu, na vrhu mešanja barv skupaj na **paleti** ali "
"celo znotraj dlak njihovih **čopičev**. Z malo prakse in know-howa, in "
"zahvaljujoč raznolikosti zmogljivih orodij v Kriti, lahko posnemamo vse te "
"tehnike mešanja v digitalnem slikanju."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:21
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In both traditional and digital painting, mixing techniques can be divided "
"into *two major categories*: let's call them **\"on-canvas\"** and **\"off-"
"canvas\"**."
msgstr ""
"V tradicionalnem in digitalnem slikanju lahko tehnike mešanja razdelimo v "
"*dve večji kategoriji*: recimo jim **\"na platnu\"** in **\"off-canvas\"**."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:24
#, fuzzy
msgid "On-Canvas Mixing"
msgstr "Mešanje na platnu"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:26
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On-canvas mixing techniques are ones where multiple colors are combined "
"directly on the canvas as the artist paints. This takes a few forms, "
"including **layering semi-transparent color** on top of another color, using "
"**texture** to change how a color is perceived, or even in the interaction "
"between two areas of wet paint in traditional media. Bottom line: on-canvas "
"mixing happens right on the canvas and is a great tool for artistic "
"exploration and \"happy accidents\"."
msgstr ""
"Tehnike mešanja na platnu so tehnike, kjer se več barv kombinira neposredno "
"na platnu, kot slika umetnik. To je nekaj oblik, vključno z **plasti pol "
"pregledno barvo** na vrhu druge barve, z uporabo **teksturo** spremeniti, "
"kako se barva dojema, ali celo v interakciji med dvema območjema vlažne "
"barve v tradicionalnih medijih. Bottom line: mešanje na platnu se dogaja "
"točno na platnu in je odlično orodje za umetniško raziskovanje in \"srečne "
"nesreče\"."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:29
#, fuzzy
msgid "Glazing"
msgstr "Zasteklitev"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:35
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In traditional painting, **glazing** is overlaying many different semi-"
"transparent layers to create on-canvas color mixtures. Likewise, in digital "
"painting we can also use glazing to mix colors directly on our canvas. This "
"is one of the most fundamental and commonly used mixing techniques in "
"digital painting."
msgstr ""
"Pri tradicionalnem slikanju * **zasteklitev** prelaga številne različne pol "
"pregledne plasti, da bi ustvarili barvne mešanice na platnu. Prav tako lahko "
"pri digitalnem slikanju uporabljamo tudi zasteklitev za mešanje barv "
"neposredno na našem platnu. To je ena najbolj temeljnih in pogosto "
"uporabljenih tehnik mešanja v digitalnem slikanju."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:37
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We first lay down a semi-transparent layer on top of another color that we "
"intend to mix with. Then, we pick the **resultant color** with the :kbd:"
"`Ctrl +` |mouseleft| shortcut (this can be configured in the canvas input "
"settings), and paint with that. Depending on our brush's **opacity "
"setting**, each time we glaze one color over another we will get a color "
"that is somewhere between those two colors, often leading to a nice mixture."
msgstr ""
"Najprej položimo pol pregledno plast na vrh druge barve, s ki jo nameravamo "
"pomešati. Nato izberemo **resultant color** z :kbd:'Ctrl +' |mouseleft| "
"bližnjico (to je mogoče konfigurirati v nastavitvah vnosa na platno) in "
"slikajte s tem. Glede na nastavitev naše krtače **nepreglednost**, vsakič, "
"ko zasteklimo eno barvo nad drugo, bomo dobili barvo, ki je nekje med temi "
"dvema barvama, ki pogosto vodi do lepe zmesi."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:39
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We can mix even more easily with glazing when we set our brush's **flow** to "
"a lower setting. Subtly different than opacity, :ref:`flow "
"<option_opacity_n_flow>` is transparency per dab instead of stroke, and so "
"it gives us softer strokes without giving up control."
msgstr ""
"Z zasteklitvijo lahko še lažje zmešamo, ko nastavimo čopičev **tok** na "
"nižjo nastavitev. Subtitno drugačna od nepreglednosti, :ref:'flow ' je "
"preglednost na dab namesto možganske kapi, in tako nam daje mehke poteze, ne "
"da bi se odrekali <option_opacity_n_flow>nadzoru."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:41
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Furthermore, we can combine glazing with various **blending modes** to "
"achieve different, interesting effects. For example, glazing with the "
"**multiply** blending mode to create nice shadows:"
msgstr ""
"Poleg tega lahko kombiniramo zasteklitev z različnimi **načini mešanja** za "
"doseganje različnih, zanimivih učinkov. Na primer, zasteklitev z načinom "
"**pomnoževanja** za ustvarjanje lepih senc:"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:46
#, fuzzy
msgid "Staring with line art and base colors."
msgstr "Strmi z line art in osnovnimi barvami."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:51
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Using a semi-transparent brush that's set to multiply, we can add colored "
"layers to suggest shadows and mid-tones. The multiply blending mode will "
"darken and interact with each base color differently."
msgstr ""
"Z uporabo pol pregledne krtače, ki je nastavljena na razmnoževanje, lahko "
"dodamo barvne plasti, ki predlagajo sence in srednje tone. Način "
"množitvenega mešanja se bo drugače temnil in interakcija z vsako osnovno "
"barvo."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:56
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Then, using a brush with low flow (~0.30), we can pick the resulting colors "
"and lay down more layers. Not only does this help you define the different "
"planes and forms that are so crucial for creating a sense of depth and three-"
"dimensionality, it also gives quite a nice, painterly effect!"
msgstr ""
"Nato lahko s čopičem z nizkim pretokom (~0,30) izberemo posledne barve in "
"položimo več plasti. Ne samo, da vam to pomaga opredeliti različne ravnine "
"in oblike, ki so tako ključnega pomena za ustvarjanje občutka globine in "
"tridimenzionalnosti, daje tudi precej lep, slikarski učinek!"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:62
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Continue with a lower opacity and flow to create even smoother gradients. "
"Make your **edges** as sharp or smooth as your subject matter and art style "
"demands!"
msgstr ""
"Nadaljujte z manjšo nepreglednost in pretok, da ustvarite še bolj gladke "
"gradiente. Naredite svoje **robove** tako ostre ali gladke, kot zahteva vaša "
"predmetna zadeva in umetnostni slog!"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:65
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Smudge"
msgid "Smudging"
msgstr "Razmaži"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:71
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Smudge mixing** is done with the :ref:`color_smudge_brush_engine`, a "
"special brush engine that allows you to mix your current brush color with "
"the color(s) under the brush. It's a very powerful type of brush that gives "
"a lovely painterly effect. *Performance wise, it's a bit more demanding and "
"slower than the regular pixel brush*."
msgstr ""
"**Smudge mešanje** se opravi z :ref:'color_smudge_brush_engine', posebnim "
"ščetkanim motorjem, ki omogoča mešanje trenutne barve čopiča z barvo(e) pod "
"čopičem. To je zelo močna vrsta čopiča, ki daje lep slikarski učinek. "
"*Performance wise, je nekoliko zahtevnejši in počasnejši od navadne ščetke "
"za piksle*."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:73
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you *remove all paint from a smudge brush*, you get a simple-yet-powerful "
"smudge effect:"
msgstr ""
"Če *odstranite vso barvo iz razmaženega čopiča*, boste dobili preprost, a "
"zmogljiv razmaženega učinka:"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:79
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Different smudge brushes have different effects, so be sure to try them all "
"out!"
msgstr ""
"Različne smudge čopiče imajo različne učinke, zato se prepričajte, da jih "
"preizkusite vse ven!"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:84
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Scumbling** is similar to glazing, except instead of having a semi-opaque "
"layer, we use layers of **textured** or **patterned** paint."
msgstr ""
"**Scumbling** je podoben zasteklitvi, le da namesto, da bi imeli pol "
"nepregledno plast, uporabljamo plasti **tekstured** ali **vzorčaste** barve."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:89
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Like most painting programs, Krita allows you to pick a :ref:"
"`option_brush_tip`, which can be used to create a textured effect like that "
"of scumbling."
msgstr ""
"Kot večina slikarskih programov vam Krita omogoča, da izberejo :"
"ref:'option_brush_tip', ki se lahko uporablja za ustvarjanje teksturo "
"učinek, kot je ta od smeti."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:95
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Krita's brush engines also allow you to use :ref:`option_texture`. This "
"allows you to create interesting and stylized screentone-like effects."
msgstr ""
"Kritini ščetkani motorji omogočajo tudi uporabo :ref:'option_texture'. To "
"vam omogoča ustvarjanje zanimivih in stiliziranih screentone podobnih "
"učinkov."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:97
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With glazing can get you pretty far when it comes to *defining planes and "
"forms*, scumbling is the best method to *create texture and to break up big "
"pasty flats* in your painting."
msgstr ""
"Z zasteklitvijo vas lahko precej daleč, ko gre za *določanje ravnin in "
"oblik*, je gnjevljenje najboljša metoda za *ustvarjanje tekstura in "
"razčlenitev velikih pasty ravnin* v vaši sliki."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:100
#, fuzzy
msgid "Off-Canvas Mixing"
msgstr "Mešanje brez platna"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:102
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"**Off-canvas** mixing has basically always been a core tool for artists "
"everywhere; when we think of the stereotypical artist we might imagine "
"someone with a few **brushes** in one hand and a wooden **palette** in the "
"other. Whether it's oils, watercolor, or other traditional media, for the "
"artist to have absolute control over their colors it's crucial to have some "
"kind of palette, plate, jar, or other **off-canvas area** to mix colors "
"together. While it's easy to overlook this in digital painting (where "
"selecting fresh new colors without mixing at all is both easy and free), "
"Krita has a few very useful and unique features for off-canvas mixing."
msgstr ""
"**Off-canvas** mešanje je bilo v bistvu vedno temeljno orodje za umetnike "
"povsod; ko pomislimo na stereotipnega umetnika, si lahko predstavljamo "
"nekoga z nekaj **čopiči** v eni roki in leseno **paleto** v drugi. Ne glede "
"na to, ali gre za olja, a watercolor ali druge tradicionalne medije, da ima "
"umetnik popoln nadzor nad svojimi barvami, je ključnega pomena, da imajo "
"nekakšno paleto, ploščo, kozarec ali drugo **off-platno območje** za mešanje "
"barv skupaj. Medtem ko je enostavno spregledati to v digitalnem slikanju "
"(kjer je izbira svežih novih barv brez mešanja na vse enostavno in "
"brezplačno), Krita ima nekaj zelo uporabnih in edinstvenih funkcij za "
"mešanje off-platno."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:105
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Color Sampler Tool"
msgid "Color Sampler Blending"
msgstr "Orodje Vzorčevalnik barv"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:109
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Krita, like almost every art and graphics program, has a :ref:"
"`color_sampler_tool` which allows you to very quickly sample a color from "
"any pixel on your canvas. While this tool may seem relatively simple and "
"humble, it is also one of the most important and commonly used tools in the "
"digital artist's toolbox - perhaps only second to the brush! In fact, the "
"color sampler tool is at the very heart of mixing colors, and is often used "
"in combination with on-canvas techniques like glazing and scumbling to "
"produce smooth blends of color."
msgstr ""
"Krita ima tako kot skoraj vsak umetniški in grafični program :"
"ref:'color_sampler_tool', ki omogoča zelo hitro vzorčenje barve iz katerega "
"koli piksla na vašem platnu. Čeprav se to orodje morda zdi razmeroma "
"preprosto in skromno, je tudi eno najpomembnejših in pogosto uporabljenih "
"orodij v orodni škatli digitalnega umetnika - morda le sekundo na čopič! "
"Pravzaprav je orodje za vzorčenje barv v središču mešanja barv in se pogosto "
"uporablja v kombinaciji s tehnikami na platnu, kot sta zasteklitev in "
"gnjevljenje, da bi ustvarili gladke mešanice barv."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:111
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"And still, there is more to this little tool than meets the eye! Not only "
"can you configure Krita's color sampler to sample from the average color of "
"a **radius** of pixels, Krita's Color Sampler also has a unique **blending** "
"feature: a powerful and intuitive tool for off-canvas color mixing!"
msgstr ""
"In še vedno je več tega malega orodja, kot se sreča z očesom! Ne samo, da "
"lahko konfigurirate Kritinega barvnega vzorčevalnika za vzorčenje iz "
"povprečne barve **polmera** pik, Krita's Color Sampler ima tudi edinstveno "
"**mešanje** funkcijo: zmogljivo in intuitivno orodje za mešanje barv brez "
"platna!"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:117
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Color Sampler Blending feature changes the way that picking colors has "
"traditionally worked for decades; instead of completely replacing your "
"current brush color with the newly sampled color, *blending allows you to "
"quickly \"soak up\" some portion of the sampled color*, which is then mixed "
"with your current brush color."
msgstr ""
"Funkcija Color Sampler Blending spreminja način, kako je izbiranje barv "
"tradicionalno delovalo desetletja; namesto, da bi v celoti nadomestili vašo "
"trenutno barvo čopiča z novo vzorčeni barvo, *mešanje vam omogoča, da hitro "
"\"namočite\" nekaj dela vzorčene barve*, ki se nato meša z vašo trenutno "
"barvo čopiča."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:119
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You can use Color Sampler Blending much like a physical paint brush in "
"traditional media. If you were to dip your paint brush into a pool of *blue* "
"paint, and then immediately dip again into a pool of *red* paint and paint a "
"stroke across your canvas, the stoke wouldn't be pure red - it would be some "
"combination of blue and red which would mix to create an intermediate purple "
"color. Which shade of purple would depend on the ratio of paints that mix "
"together within the hairs of your brush, and this is essentially what the "
"Color Sampler's \"blend\" option controls: what percentage of sampled color "
"is mixed together with your current brush color!"
msgstr ""
"Color Sampler Blending lahko uporabite podobno kot fizična čopič barve v "
"tradicionalnih medijih. Če bi ščetko za barvo namočili v bazen *modre* "
"barve, nato pa takoj ponovno namočite v bazen *rdeče* barve in pobarvajte "
"potezo po platnu, stoke ne bi bilo čisto rdeče - to bi bila neka kombinacija "
"modre in rdeče, ki bi zmešala, da bi ustvarila vmesno vijolično barvo. "
"Kateri odmerek vijolične barve bi bil odvisen od razmerja barv, ki se mešajo "
"skupaj znotraj dlak vašega čopiča, in to je v bistvu tisto, kar color "
"Sampler's \"blend\" možnost nadzoruje: kakšen odstotek vzorčene barve se "
"meša skupaj z vašo trenutno barvo čopiča!"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:121
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Not only does Krita's Color Sampler Blending feel even more like mixing "
"paints, it is also completely off-canvas and independent of opacity, flow, "
"shape, and other brush settings. Furthermore, unlike most on-canvas mixing "
"techniques, Color Sampler Blending works regardless of the location of "
"colors on your canvas - enabling you to mix with colors at any position, on "
"any layer, or even in different documents! Quickly mix lighting colors with "
"local colors, mix the ambient sky color into shadows, create atmospheric "
"depth, mix from a preselected palette of colors in another layer/document, "
"etc."
msgstr ""
"Ne samo, da krita's Color Sampler Blending počutijo še bolj kot mešanje "
"barv, je tudi popolnoma off-platno in neodvisno od nepreglednosti, pretoka, "
"oblike in drugih nastavitev čopiča. Poleg tega, za razliko od večine tehnik "
"mešanja na platnu, Color Sampler Blending deluje ne glede na lokacijo barv "
"na vašem platnu - ki vam omogoča mešanje z barvami na kateri koli poziciji, "
"na kateri koli plasti, ali celo v različnih dokumentih! Hitro zmešamo "
"svetlobne barve z lokalnimi barvami, zmešamo barvo ambientalnega neba v "
"sence, ustvarimo atmosfersko globino, zmešamo iz vnaprej določene palete "
"barv v drugi plasti/dokumentu itd."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:123
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To use Color Sampler Blending, simply set the \"blend\" option in the **Tool "
"Options Docker** while the Color Sampler Tool is active; setting blend to "
"100% will cause your Color Sampler to work in the traditional way "
"(completely replacing your brush color with the picked color), setting to "
"around 50% will give you a half-way mix between colors, and setting to a "
"lower value will create more subtle shifts in colors each click. Of course, "
"blending affects both your dedicated Color Sampler Tool as well as the :kbd:"
"`Ctrl +` |mouseleft| shortcut."
msgstr ""
"Če želite uporabiti barvno vzorčenje, preprosto nastavite možnost »mešanica« "
"v dockerju **Tool Options Docker** medtem ko je orodje za vzorčenje barv "
"aktivno; nastavitev mešanice na 100% bo povzročila, da bo vaš Color Sampler "
"deloval na tradicionalen način (popolnoma zamenjavo barve čopiča z izbirčno "
"barvo), nastavitev na okoli 50% vam bo dala napol mešanico med barvami, in "
"nastavitev na nižjo vrednost bo ustvarila bolj subtile premike v barvah vsak "
"klik. Seveda, mešanje vpliva tako na vaš namen color sampler Tool, kot tudi "
"na :kbd:'Ctrl +' |mouseleft| bližnjica."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:127
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Clicking and dragging the Color Sampler around the canvas currently causes "
"it to sample many times as it switches pixels. You can use this trait to "
"quickly soak up more color by \"dipping\" your color sampler into color and "
"swirling it around. This can be pretty satisfying! However, this also means "
"that some care must be taken to prevent from accidentally picking up more "
"color than you want. It's pretty easy to click a single pixel only one time "
"using a **mouse**, but when painting with a **drawing tablet and pen** it "
"can sometimes be desirable to use a slightly lower blend setting!"
msgstr ""
"Če kliknete in povlečete barvni vzorčnik okoli platna, ga trenutno večkrat "
"vzorči, ko preklopi pike. To lahko uporabite, da hitro namočite več barve "
"tako, da \"potapljate\" svoj barvni vzorč v barvo in jo zamahnete okoli. To "
"je lahko precej zadovoljivo! Vendar to pomeni tudi, da je treba paziti, da "
"ne bi po nesreči pobrali več barve, kot si želite. To je precej enostavno, "
"da kliknete eno pikslo samo enkrat z uporabo **miške**, vendar pri slikanju "
"z **risanje tablete in peresa** je včasih zaželeno, da uporabite nekoliko "
"nižjo nastavitev mešanice!"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:130
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Digital Colors Mixer"
msgid "The Digital Colors Mixer"
msgstr "Digitalni mešalnik barv"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:132
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Somewhat hidden away in the **Dockers** menu (:menuselection:`Settings --> "
"Dockers --> Digital Colors Mixer`), this can be a useful tool for off-canvas "
"mixing. The Digital Colors Mixer looks a little bit like an audio mixing "
"board that you'd see in a recording studio, but instead of mixing music it "
"mixes colors! It contains 6 independent **color mixers** that mix your "
"current brush color with any color of your choosing."
msgstr ""
"Nekoliko skrito v meniju **Dockers** (:menuselection:'Nastavitve --> Dockers "
"--> Digital Colors Mixer'), je to lahko uporabno orodje za mešanje brez "
"platna. Digital Colors Mixer je videti nekoliko kot zvočna mešalni deska, ki "
"bi jo videli v studiu za snemanje, vendar namesto mešanja glasbe meša barve! "
"Vsebuje 6 neodvisnih **barvnih mešalcev** ki zmešajo vašo trenutno barvo "
"čopiča s katerokoli barvo po vaši izbiri."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:138
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"By clicking the **color buttons** below each mixer you can choose a palette "
"of colors to mix with. Above each mixer is a **color patch** that will "
"produce a color that mixes some amount of your current brush color with the "
"palette color. Colors towards the top of the mixer will deliver subtle "
"changes to your current color, while colors towards the bottom will be much "
"closer to the palette color of that channel."
msgstr ""
"S klikom na **barvne gumbe** pod vsakim mešalnikom lahko izberete paleto "
"barv, s katero se lahko pomešate. Nad vsakim mešalnikom je **barvni obliž** "
"ki bo proizvedla barvo, ki bo z barvo palete zmešala nekaj količine vaše "
"trenutne barve čopiča. Barve proti vrhu mešalnika bodo prinašale subtile "
"spremembe trenutne barve, medtem ko bodo barve proti dnu veliko bližje "
"paletni barvi tega kanala."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:141
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Other"
msgid "Other Tips"
msgstr "Drugo"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:143
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Outside of making it easier to create smooth gradients, mixing has another "
"benefit: It allows you to create a cohesive piece."
msgstr ""
"Poleg lažjega ustvarjanja gladkih gradientov ima mešanje še eno korist: "
"Omogoča ustvarjanje kohezivnega kosa."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:145
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Limiting the number of colors we use and then mixing tends to give a more "
"cohesive palette, as we're not trying to do too much at once. This cohesive "
"palette in turn means it will become easier to create a certain mood in an "
"image. Sometimes, mixing in a little bit of accent color can also create "
"unexpected results which in turn can be a little discovery for the audience "
"to delight over as they discover the world of your image."
msgstr ""
"Omejevanje števila barv, ki jih uporabljamo, in potem mešanje, ima na voljo "
"bolj kohezivno paleto, saj ne poskušamo storiti preveč naenkrat. Ta "
"kohezivna paleta pa pomeni, da bo postalo lažje ustvariti določeno "
"razpoloženje na sliki. Včasih lahko mešanje v malo barve naglasa ustvari "
"tudi nepričakovane rezultate, ki pa so lahko majhno odkritje za občinstvo, "
"da se navdušenje nad, ko odkrijejo svet vaše podobe."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:147
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"What we can learn from this, is that the next time we select, say, gray, "
"instead of reaching for a random or generic gray from the Advanced Color "
"Selector, consider using one of Krita's many wonderful mixing tools to "
"create an interesting and fitting gray from hues that are roughly "
"complementary (opposite each other on the hue wheel)."
msgstr ""
"Iz tega se lahko naučimo, da naslednjič, ko izberemo, na primer, sivo, "
"namesto da bi segali po naključni ali generični sivi iz naprednega izbirnika "
"barv, razmislite o uporabi enega izmed številnih čudovitih mešalnih orodij "
"Krite, da ustvarite zanimivo in prilegajoče sivo barvo iz odtenkov, ki so "
"približno komplementarni (nasproti drug drugemu na kolesu odtenka)."

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:149
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"While on-canvas and off-canvas techniques are fundamentally different "
"categories of mixing colors, they are not mutually exclusive. All of the "
"mixing methods in this article have pros and cons; different tools can be "
"useful for different situations, and combining various techniques can be "
"extremely powerful and fun!"
msgstr ""
"Medtem ko so tehnike na platnu in off-platnu v osnovi različne kategorije "
"mešanja barv, se medsebojno ne izključujejo. Vse metode mešanja v tem članku "
"imajo prednosti in slabosti; različna orodja so lahko uporabna za različne "
"situacije, združevanje različnih tehnik pa je lahko izjemno zmogljivo in "
"zabavno!"

#: ../../general_concepts/colors/color_mixing.rst:151
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Finally, mixing colors will often go far better in a :ref:`higher bit-depth "
"like 16bit <bit_depth>`, though it'll make the image take up much more "
"working **memory** (RAM). Furthermore, using a :ref:`linear color space "
"<linear_and_gamma>` can often give far better mixtures than a **gamma-"
"corrected** one, though doing sketches and line art is easier to do in a "
"gamma-corrected space."
msgstr ""
"Nazadnje, mešanje barv bo pogosto šel veliko bolje v :ref:'višja bit-globina "
"kot 16bit ', čeprav bo slika zajel veliko bolj delovno <bit_depth>**spomin** "
"(RAM). Poleg tega lahko uporaba :ref:'linearnega barvnega prostora ' pogosto "
"daje veliko boljše zmesi kot <linear_and_gamma>**gama-popravljena** ena, "
"čeprav je delo skic in line art lažje narediti v gama-popravljenem prostoru."
